<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea oil exports dip, crude main lose.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea oil exports dip, crude main lose.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of crude and refined oil products from the Baltic and Black Sea fell by 80,499 barrels per day (bpd) in the last week of May to 1.51 million bpd, Petro-Logistics Ltd said.</p>
<p>Crude and fuel oil exports both dipped while gas oil, gasoline and jet, and naphtha exports increased.</p>
<p>The total was 483,842 bpd lower than in the same week last year, the Geneva-based consultancy which tracks tanker movements said.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics is a breakdown of oil exports from the Baltic and the Black Sea in the last week of May (in bpd):</p>
<p>		  Crude oil   Fuel Oil   Gasoil   Mogas/Jet   Total</p>
<p>Total FSU	784,950    388,990    305,931   10,218</p>
<p>1,510,417</p>
<p>Rom/Bul					103,459   29,942</p>
<p>133,401</p>
<p>Total tonnes   784,950    388,990    409,390   40,610</p>
<p>1,643,818</p>
<p>Total bpd	817,469    359,816    435,416   47,861</p>
<p>1,686,118</p>
<p>Change on wk  -192,758    -25,578   +110,837   +1,444</p>
<p>-80,499</p>
<p>Change on yr  -371,016   -152,741    +46,093  +17,728</p>
<p>-483,842</p>
<p>Note: Naphtha exports were 25,556 bpd up on last week when they were zero, but 23,906 bpd down on the same week last year. -- London newsroom, +44 171 542 7714</p>
</text>
